# =============================================================================
# agentic-patterns-ts — environment contract
# =============================================================================
# This file is version-controlled and holds SECRET REFERENCES, not values.
#
#   pts secrets set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY     # store the value in the backend
#   pts secrets check                     # verify every ref here resolves
#   pts secrets env                       # write resolved values -> .env.local (chmod 600)
#
# Backend is configured in patterns.yaml (secrets.backend: 1password,
# vault: agentic-patterns-ts). `secret://NAME` resolves to
# op://agentic-patterns-ts/NAME/password.
#
# Precedence: pts reads .env as the base, then overlays any secret://
# or op:// refs from THIS file. Plain values below fill in only if absent
# from .env.
#
# Every ref below is COMMENTED on purpose: an uncommented ref whose vault item
# you don't have fails the entire `pts secrets env` resolve. Enable the ones you
# use in your own (gitignored) `.env` — pts resolves `secret://` refs found
# there too — and leave this file as the catalogue of what's available.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Anthropic (direct API) ---------------------------------------------------
# Commented by default. Heads-up if you also use the Claude Code runners: the
# `claude` binary treats ANTHROPIC_API_KEY as taking precedence over a stored
# claude.ai login, so exporting it switches CC subprocess runs from
# subscription billing to per-token API billing. Enable it when you want the
# direct API; leave it unset to run the CC path on a subscription.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=secret://ANTHROPIC_API_KEY

# --- Claude Code harness runner (#387) — the preferred Anthropic path ---------
# resolveOAuthToken() reads (1) an explicit option, (2) this env var, (3) the
# macOS Keychain (Max subscription). On macOS nothing needs setting; set this
# for isolated-mode runs elsewhere. Generate with: claude setup-token
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=secret://CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN

# --- Langfuse (optional — #388 native cost view verification) ----------------
# Read by the Langfuse SDK where you construct the client for LangfuseExporter.
# LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=secret://LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY
# LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=secret://LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY
# LANGFUSE_BASEURL=https://cloud.langfuse.com

# --- Other providers (optional — #390 live capability probes) ----------------
# OPENAI_API_KEY=secret://OPENAI_API_KEY
# GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=secret://GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=secret://OPENROUTER_API_KEY
# XAI_API_KEY=secret://XAI_API_KEY
# GROQ_API_KEY=secret://GROQ_API_KEY
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=secret://MISTRAL_API_KEY
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=secret://DEEPSEEK_API_KEY

# --- Ollama (local GPU, no key) ----------------------------------------------
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434

# --- Gateway (Bifrost / any OpenAI-compatible endpoint) ----------------------
# Setting AP_GATEWAY_BASE_URL routes EVERY agent's declared model through the
# one gateway — no per-provider key needed. Auth is EITHER HTTP Basic OR a
# bearer key. NOTE: the findtempo dev Bifrost has no Claude models — use a
# direct ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for Anthropic work.
# AP_GATEWAY_BASE_URL=https://bifrost.internal/v1
# AP_GATEWAY_BASIC_USER=admin
# AP_GATEWAY_BASIC_PASS=secret://AP_GATEWAY_BASIC_PASS
# AP_GATEWAY_API_KEY=secret://AP_GATEWAY_API_KEY   # bearer alternative to Basic
# AP_GATEWAY_MODEL_PREFIX=anthropic/               # optional id prefix

# --- Tier: opus | sonnet | haiku (framework default: sonnet) ------------------
# AGENT_TIER=sonnet
# AGENT_MODEL=<exact-id>   # wins over AGENT_TIER; both are GLOBAL overrides
